# How these pins were produced (reproduce exactly, from any machine):
#   git clone --depth 1 "$UPSTREAM_URL" upstream-wallet
#   cd upstream-wallet && git rev-parse HEAD          # must equal UPSTREAM_SHA
#   git -c core.autocrlf=false -c core.eol=lf archive --format=tar HEAD | tar -x -C <dest>
#   # then remove the three files listed above; repeat for STANDALONE_URL
# core.autocrlf MUST be disabled: on Windows a plain checkout — and `git archive`
# itself — rewrites every text file to CRLF, which changes every checksum here.
# This is not theoretical. It bit twice: once vendoring the wallet, and again on
# 2026-08-09 vendoring this standalone repo, whose LICENSE (byte-identical to the
# wallet's) came out of a default clone as eb2c5d88… instead of bbc8b96c….
